The relevant canonical threat is T-041 (prefix-cache and SSD tier, SEC-035), under TB-007. The base docs state that:
- benchmark runners use isolated, owned cache roots and keys;
- persistent test namespaces forbid ephemeral fallback;
- no production cache roots or keys are used;
- no key bytes are exported.

No cross-file interaction with enforced code was observable. A later pass should confirm that any head edits to this file do not:
- encourage using production KEKs or cache roots in tests;
- loosen the 30-minute TTL or the account-scoped cacheSalt guarantees;
- weaken the stated isolation controls (DARKBLOOM_PREFIX_CACHE_ALLOW_EPHEMERAL, DARKBLOOM_PREFIX_CACHE_TEST_ROOT, DARKBLOOM_PREFIX_CACHE_TEST_PERSISTENT_KEY).

I report no findings.
